 "issue": 2923,
 "what": "Every table read out of the plugins of the load order, in the order they read each other. scripts/mods/Rebuild-ContentTables.ps1 runs them after a change to one of Thornswood's own plugins (game/content). tests/test-2923-own-plugins.js holds the list to the builders: every builder that reads a load order is a step here or is in notInChain with its reason, and no step reads a table a later step writes.",
 "fields": "tool is the builder. data and plugins are the names it takes the game's Data folder and the plugin list by (null: it takes none). reads are the tables it reads that a builder writes; readsBack is one it reads and a later step writes back; when that step changes it (Write-CutItems.js sorting a new plugin's recipes, #4087), Rebuild-ContentTables.ps1 runs the chain again from the reader, once. writes are what it writes. uses are the other files (or a folder of them, as game/gamemode, the gamemode's source) of the repository it reads that no builder writes, outside scripts, game/content, game/data and records (#3425: Build-SpellTable.ps1 reads the K panel's book in game/ui, which was named nowhere, so scripts/mods/Run-OnBox.ps1 never sent it and the box run stopped there); tests/test-2923-own-plugins.js reads each builder for such a file and holds this list to it. writesOffChain are what its builder writes only when it is run by hand with an option the chain does not give it (Build-NpcPopulation.py --write-runtime, #3120): they are written LF like a step's writes, and are not sent to the box or brought back.",
 "orderProofRule": "For these JSON outputs, the source must give the count and ordered-name hash measured by the builder. Phase means the step's order before or after the Last plugin. Masters means just the five masters.",
